  "result": "The fix works. Summary of changes to `src/click/testing.py`:\n\n- Replaced `BytesIOCopy`'s `io.BytesIO` backing with a real `tempfile.TemporaryFile`, so it exposes a genuine `fileno()` \u2014 this is what `subprocess.run(..., stdout=sys.stdout)` (or `stderr`) needs instead of raising `io.UnsupportedOperation`. Added `getvalue()` (seek/read/restore-position) and `__getattr__` delegation to preserve the existing `io.BytesIO`-like interface used elsewhere (e.g. `.closed`).\n- Added `__del__` to close the underlying temp file on garbage collection (avoiding `ResourceWarning`s in tests that construct `BytesIOCopy`/`StreamMixer` directly).\n- Explicitly close `stream_mixer.stdout`/`stderr`'s underlying temp files in `CliRunner.isolation`'s `finally` block after the captured values have been read, so `CliRunner.invoke()` doesn't leak file descriptors.\n\nVerified:\n- The original SSCCE (`subprocess.run([\"echo\", \"foo\"], stdout=sys.stderr)` inside a `CliRunner`-invoked command) now succeeds and correctly captures `foo\\n` in `result.stderr`.\n- Full existing test suite (`python -m pytest tests/`) passes: 1419 passed, 24 skipped, 1 xfailed, no failures or resource warnings.",
